                "evidence": "# Integration Plan — 2026-11-02\n\n## Verdict: PROCEED\n\nThe design shows three Screens (Today, All reminders, Done). Every field they display (`title`, `due`, `done`) comes from `GET /api/reminders`, and the only action (Done) is served by `POST /api/reminders/{id}/done`. The Done Screen is a filter on `done === true` of the same data, so no new backend is needed. Blockers: 0. No adapters needed. No design-only actions.\n\n## Blockers\n- none\n\n## Needs Stakeholder decision\n- none\n\n## Not checked\n- none\n\n## Screens (Scenario C)\n| Screen | Export file | Target template | Data it displays | Actions | Backend source |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Today | `.ui-workflow/export/src/App.tsx#today` | `app/templates/index.html#today` | title, due | Done | `GET /api/reminders` (filter `done` false); `POST /api/reminders/{id}/done` |\n| All reminders | `.ui-workflow/export/src/App.tsx#all` | `app/templates/index.html#all` | title, due, done | Done (unfinished only) | `GET /api/reminders`; `POST /api/reminders/{id}/done` |\n| Done | `.ui-workflow/export/src/App.tsx#done` | `app/templates/index.html` (new `#done` view; Stakeholder must-have) | title, due | none | `GET /api/reminders` (filter `done` true, computed in the frontend) |\n\nNotes for the port:\n- The design has no Settings tab. Settings is \"not redesigned\" and must keep working, so the port must keep a way to reach it.\n- The design drops the \"Hello {{ owner }}\" greeting and the logo. Neither is Required behaviour; confirm with the Stakeholder when showing each Screen.\n\n## Next step\nRun `/ui-workflow-skills:design-port`.\n"
